    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c15cfa11_8b3c3e6d",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/lowmemorykiller.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-30T16:19:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so if we \"fill up\", when reading the proc file, we will have stale data?  Shouldn\u0027t we drop the old data instead and keep it full with the most recent information?\n\nOr am I mistaken as to how this is used?\n\nI guess I don\u0027t know how this is going to be used due to the lack of a detailed changelog comment :)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "f3fd8624bc7a9eb3676ebdeee7bdbdc666c0e0b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "557974f9_3d7f3289",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/lowmemorykiller.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003913
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-30T17:07:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a fallback so if userland stops polling/reading the file, a loss of events is preferable to continuous memory loss as the buffer continues to fill.",
      "parentUuid": "c15cfa11_8b3c3e6d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "f3fd8624bc7a9eb3676ebdeee7bdbdc666c0e0b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c511d36_a5310250",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/lowmemorykiller.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-01T10:47:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not saying constantly consume memory, but just drop the older events and only keep the new ones?\n\nIt\u0027s a trade off, do you want to miss old events, or new ones.  It\u0027s your call, you are in charge of the userspace side of this :)",
      "parentUuid": "557974f9_3d7f3289",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "f3fd8624bc7a9eb3676ebdeee7bdbdc666c0e0b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91e2f929_bf142dae",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/lowmemorykiller.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003913
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-01T13:30:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The logic is that if userland has stopped reading the messages then something has gone very wrong, we give up on the metrics and the priority is not crashing the device. All metrics are equally useful, it is not like more recently metrics would be more prized.",
      "parentUuid": "3c511d36_a5310250",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "f3fd8624bc7a9eb3676ebdeee7bdbdc666c0e0b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
